# Serving the page a seed lands on — on a host that reads this file.
#
# **peacegarden.app does not.** The live vhost on 20i is nginx talking straight
# to PHP-FPM with no Apache anywhere in the chain, so nothing here is read and
# nothing here fires. That was checked on 4 September 2026 rather than assumed:
# a `RewriteRule` to a known-good path stayed a 404 and a `Header always set`
# never appeared, at the document root and one directory down. The symptom
# without that check is at the far end and looks like a broken page — `/s`
# arrives as `application/octet-stream` and the browser saves it.
#
# The file is kept, and rewritten, because the failure was silent once and
# would be silent again if the host ever changed under us. What it now does is
# route the same four extensionless paths to `index.php`, which is what serves
# them on the live host. One mechanism, two kinds of host, rather than two
# mechanisms that could disagree about what `/s` is.
#
# `/s` is the path every seed link already points at, and the path the
# association file claims. It is a path with no extension for the same reason
# the association file is: the path is the format, and a path with `.html` on
# the end would be a different path from the one already minted into links and
# registered as an App Clip prefix. A directory called `s` with an `index.html`
# in it would cost a redirect from `/s` to `/s/` on every arrival — nginx's own
# directory redirect, which on this host answers `http://`, so it would also
# cost a plaintext hop. A fragment survives a redirect; the plaintext hop is
# not worth taking on the one path this whole site exists to answer.

<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
    RewriteEngine On
    RewriteRule ^(s|g|t)$ index.php [L]
    RewriteRule ^\.well-known/apple-app-site-association$ index.php [L]
</IfModule>

AddDefaultCharset utf-8

# The passage banks and the language manifest are generated by
# `tools/site/export.py` and served as they are written. nginx types these from
# its own `mime.types` and gets them right without being told; this is for a
# host that does not.
<IfModule mod_mime.c>
    AddType application/json .json
</IfModule>

# `.pages/` holds the four files this routes to, off the paths they are served
# at. nginx refuses dot-directories itself; Apache is told to here.
<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
    <Directory ".pages">
        Require all denied
    </Directory>
</IfModule>

# What this file cannot do, said here rather than assumed:
#
# **Request logging.** docs/WEBSITE.md asks for no request log on `/s`, or the
# shortest one the host permits. That is a setting in the 20i control panel
# rather than a directive here, so it is a deploy step — see Server/README.md.
# Nothing on this page should claim more than what is actually switched off.
#
# **Robots.** No directive here, deliberately. `noindex` is settled for shared
# plant pages, which publish somebody's name beside a line about a real
# meeting. This page publishes nothing: with a seed in it the content is in the
# fragment, which a crawler never receives, and with no seed it is the page
# that says what Peace Garden is. Whether the site is ever *meant* to be found
# in a search engine is an open question in docs/WEBSITE.md, and it is a
# question about a marketing page rather than about seeds.
